<title>UK: London tea auction finds good demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction finds good demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good demand was seen for landed teas at the latest auction by the Tea Brokers' Association of London.</p>
<p>The limited quantity of Kenya teas on offer were firm to dearer but other East Africans declined 2 to 4 pence. Coloury Central Africans often advanced.</p>
<p>Offshore teas found strong competition at dearer rates.</p>
</text>
